  "id": "Compound::DB00393 - Gene::785",
  "verbalization": "Nimodipine, a calcium channel blocker, is shown to interact with multiple members of the Cacna1 family, including Cacna1s, Cacnb1, and Cacna1f, which are all involved in high-voltage-gated calcium channel activity. This suggests that Nimodipine may exert its effects through a common mechanism involving calcium channel regulation. The evidence indicates that Nimodipine binds to these channels, modulating their activity, and that this activity is linked to Cacnb4, a key component of the calcium channel complex. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential role for Nimodipine in influencing calcium homeostasis through the Cacna1 family, with Cacnb4 being a central player in this process. The strong binding scores and the shared participation in high-voltage-gated calcium channel activity support a mechanistic link between Nimodipine and Cacnb4, though further experimental validation is needed to confirm the direct interaction and functional significance.",
